# Regenerated output and private key material. Neither belongs in git:
#   *.key      — these are throwaway test keys, but a private key in a repository is a
#                private key in a repository, and the admission scanner has a critical
#                pattern for exactly that. The certificates are public; the keys are not.
#   .build/    — scratch trees the harnesses write and rewrite on every run, including the
#                certificates generated against today's date.
#   *.crt      — only the two fixtures pinned to FIXED dates are committed: exp3 (expired
#                2021) and fut (not valid until 2030), which cannot be generated relative to
#                today. Every other certificate is build output under .build/certs now —
#                generating them into this directory rewrote ten committed files on every
#                test run, which dirtied the working tree and made open_catalog_pr.sh refuse
#                to run until they were restored.
*.key
*.csr
*.srl
.build/
__pycache__/